  "label": "The text 'and that's why i gas people' maps onto Adolf Hitler as the perpetrator of genocide.",
  "description": "The textual element 'and that's why i gas people' is an analogical mapping that projects Adolf Hitler (the visual entity) as the cause or reason for the vulgar pun. The text implies that Hitler is responsible for the act of 'gassing' people, equating his historical role in the Holocaust (which involved gas chambers) with a crude, modern slang meaning of 'gas'. This mapping is hateful and offensive, as it trivializes genocide by associating it with a vulgar joke. The visual material (Adolf_Hitler) is mapped onto the textual concept of a genocidal perpetrator whose actions are being mocked.",
